From c6b12b3612c8c8db7a21a9ebf4e90e71b7c983e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mitzev <ogi@kunasystems.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 21:27:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.41: generics on class header (1.01 #1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Classes with generic parameters (lifetime, type, or const) now
compile. Before this patch, any `class Foo<A> { ... }` ICEd
at ast_lowering with "duplicate copy of DefId(Foo::A) in
lctx.children" because both HIR halves (Struct + Impl) tried to
claim the same generic-param DefId.

Root cause: P09.39 had a single `generics: Generics` on
`ast::Class`, shared between the struct half and the synthetic
inherent impl half. When each half's `lower_generics` call
registered HIR children for the params, the DefIds collided.

Fix: give the impl half its own parallel `Generics` value
(`ast::Class::impl_generics`), emitted as a clone of the
parsed `generics` with all-dummy NodeIds — expansion's
`visit_id` then assigns fresh distinct NodeIds during the
normal pass. This matches how a hand-written `impl<A> Foo<A>`
has DefIds separate from the struct's.

Downstream:
- rustc_resolve: new `resolve_class` two-phase walk. Struct
  half's generic-param rib scopes the fields; impl half's rib
  scopes the self-type and methods. Mirrors
  resolve_adt + resolve_implementation composed.
- rustc_resolve/def_collector: walks `impl_generics` under the
  impl def parent so its params get DefIds owned by the impl.
- rustc_ast_lowering: `lower_class_impl_half` uses
  `class.impl_generics` for the impl's generic-param lowering;
  struct half's generics unchanged.
- rustc_ast/visit: walks `impl_generics` alongside `generics`
  so expansion's `visit_id` sees both copies separately.
- rustc_parse: `build_cxx_class_self_path` handles const-generic
  args as `GenericArg::Const(AnonConst)` instead of the P09.30
  type-path stub (which ICEd typeck); const generics now round-trip
  correctly.

Validation:
- /tmp/p09-41-class-const-generics: type-generic
  `Pair<i32, &str>` passes; const-generic `Array<const N: usize>`
  passes with `sum() == 10`.
- /tmp/p09-39-itemkind-class: basic + single inheritance still
  green (no regression).
- rustcc workspace: cargo test --workspace → 235/0.
